I would say that there's increasing emphasis on using Finite Element Method.<br><br>It has always been used for structural analysis with varying precision in the old days to be fast enough to calculate.<br>It can be approximately done in real time now, but the problem of optimization still has more room to go.<br><br>I really want to try it out, but I have yet to find many usable implementations that are opensource and general purpose. <br>I think xissburg is working on this.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="https://pybullet.org/Bullet/phpBB3/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=8992">kloplop321</a> — Thu Feb 16, 2012 7:27 pm</p><hr />
